What qstack takes from pstack:

  - The architecture: a routing skill whose playbooks are copied into a
    todolist verbatim, short model-only principle leaf skills that are cited
    when they change a decision, a SessionStart hook that injects the routing
    mandate, and project playbooks that extend bundled ones by anchoring to
    quoted step text.
  - skills/principle-test-behavior-not-implementation adapts pstack's
    principle of the same name.

Everything else in qstack (the QA playbooks, the other principles, the
shift-left pipeline, the guard hook, the agents, the references, and the
scripts) is original to qstack.
